</element-citation></ref></ref-list></back><floats-group><fig position="float" id="f1-cise-2025-00500"><label>Fig. 1.</label><caption><p>A 14-year-old male with a sports-related right midshaft clavicle fracture. (A) Initial injury radiograph demonstrated a minimally displaced fracture with apex cranial angulation and no associated soft tissue swelling or pneumothorax. (B) Six-week follow-up radiograph demonstrated interval healing with early callus formation and persistent cranial angulation. (C) Radiograph at 3 months post-injury demonstrated osseous union with restoration of clavicular length and contour.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="cise-2025-00500f1" position="float"/></fig></floats-group></article>